Subject: Cantor Attention Manifest Refresh P6 Adversarial Validation Addendum

@ [research_uuid] f8512163-d6cc-4dbc-97de-7585d0f60eb3
@ [date] 2026-09-02

& [Purpose]
  + test whether P6 validators reject structurally valid-looking substitutions rather than only accepting happy-path canonical forms

& [Adversaries]
  + unknown field injected into a serialized manifest window
  + supported shape with unsupported manifest-window profile
  + changed display label without recomputing the manifest and window digest chain
  + changed materialized mutable state under the original record and materialization digests
  + substituted host result under an otherwise valid request response envelope
  + repeated equal host request at equal journal head

& [Result]
  + every unknown profile digest body and result substitution refuses
  + equal host requests at an equal journal head replay to exactly equal zero-successor transitions
  + the focused P6 fixture now passes seven of seven including capacity coverage cost scaling staleness MCP correspondence and adversarial validation

& [Interpretation]
  + the P6 seam is not merely descriptive context formatting; it has independently replayed correspondence checks at the object manifest window materialization receipt and host-result layers

& [Nonclaims]
  + validation proves internal consistency with admitted current state and does not prove external truth model comprehension or effect correctness
